      "title": "Component 2 study note / Using a queue",
      "heading": "Using a queue",
      "url": "https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/datastructures.html#using-lists-as-queues",
      "text": "A queue serves items in first-in, first-out (FIFO) order. Enqueue appends to the back, and dequeue removes the oldest item from the front."
    },
    {
      "id": "cs-4",
      "source": "cs-4",
      "title": "Component 2 study note / Using a stack",
      "heading": "Using a stack",
      "url": "https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/datastructures.html#using-lists-as-stacks",
      "text": "A stack keeps items in last-in, first-out order. Push adds an item to the top of the stack. Pop removes the most recently pushed item from the top."
    }
