        "id": "sort-1",
        "source": "sort-1",
        "title": "Component 2 study note / Insertion sort",
        "heading": "Insertion sort",
        "url": "https://xlinux.nist.gov/dads/HTML/insertionSort.html",
        "text": "Insertion sort grows an ordered region. For each successive unsorted item, compare it with items already ordered and insert it in its proper position. Shifting or swapping preceding items can make room."
      },
      {
        "id": "sort-2",
        "source": "sort-2",
        "title": "Component 2 study note / Selection sort",
        "heading": "Selection sort",
        "url": "https://xlinux.nist.gov/dads/HTML/selectionSort.html",
        "text": "Selection sort repeatedly chooses the smallest value from the unsorted remainder and puts it in the next position of the sorted result. Swapping the chosen item into place is one implementation. Reversing the comparison selects the largest remaining item for descending order."
      }
